 "carriedNotes": {
  "R2-1": "the layer pins each edge record's exact key set (schema v2 additions per record)",
  "R4-1": "the HE-002S PR body publishes the HE-002S design (its section 2, 5 and 6 are the shares' source); recorded in the HE-002S design's flow",
  "R4-2": "Q-HE2S-8 also amends Q-HE2S-4 (no_new_privs moves into stage 1), as the shares already state",
  "R4-3": "HE-008's SEC-4 share restates plan v2's SEC-3, which HE-008 owns; HI-7's start-state list is narrower than the seal's accepted states, which is harmless as an obligation",
  "HE-002S-D2": "HE-002S design review round 3, D2: HE-008's share lists only dir search and file open and read for /proc/self/status; reading it also needs search on /proc, read on the /proc/self link and getattr on the file (and directory open and read, depending on the opener). Under the shareRule a share adds and never narrows, so HE-008's design completes the list",
  "Q-HE2S-9": "Owner decision Q-HE2S-9 (a), 2026-10-13: the signed I04 port is 1024 or above, so kept is always empty and the gate holds no capability after the seal. HE-003's share: kept is always empty, and HE-003's configuration check refuses a lower port. HE-008's share: the accepted start states lose CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE (the full root set, or a start within {CAP_SETPCAP}).",
  "Q-HE2S-10": "Owner decision Q-HE2S-10 (a), 2026-10-13: section 4.3 is amended so the gate qualifies the broker by label, cgroup, pidfd/start time and SO_PEERCRED; the broker's artifact identity comes from the observer's native-profile record (HE-004). Carried to the HE-003 and HE-005 designs and to the section 4.3 owner; the amendment vehicle is named later."
 },
